# Day 46

## Experiment Title

Monitoring Workflow Execution in GitHub Actions


## Objective

To study workflow execution monitoring and analyze workflow logs in GitHub Actions.


## Theory

GitHub Actions provides monitoring features that allow developers to observe workflow execution, build status, testing activity, and deployment processes. Workflow logs help developers identify errors and troubleshoot issues during automation.

Monitoring workflows improves software reliability and ensures that Continuous Integration and deployment tasks execute correctly.


## Requirements

GitHub Account

GitHub Repository

GitHub Actions

Windows Operating System


## Procedure

Open the GitHub repository.

Access the GitHub Actions section.

Observe workflow execution details and build status.

Analyze workflow logs generated during execution.

Identify successful and failed workflow stages.

Verify the completion status of automated tasks.


## Output

Workflow execution details were monitored successfully.

GitHub Actions displayed logs and automation activity correctly.

Workflow status and execution stages were verified successfully.


## Result

Successfully monitored workflow execution and analyzed logs in GitHub Actions.
